> Due to the way inla is coded internally, the easiest way to access
> smoother spde model is to build your own precision matrix as part of
> an “rgeneric” model. That is how e.g. the “barrier model” has been
> implemented, and how we are working to get more general spatial-
> temporal models.  I think there are some rgeneric examples linked
> from r-inla.org <http://r-inla.org>. You can follow the Lindgren et al 2011 paper for the
> definition of the precision for the higher order models, and use
> inla.mesh.fem() to access the needed c0, g1, g2, g3, etc matrices.
>
> Finn
>
