References: <E93itydb0kc.yfU0ADpXBgAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/E93itydb0kc/m/0jcEZtVaAAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

There is nothing that prevent you of having multiple observations of
the same unit. You just repeat the index, like

y ~ ... + f(idx, model="bym")

idx = c(1,1,2,2,2, ...)

so there are 2 observation of region 1, 3 of region 2, etc..

If that help...

H

