It appears from here <https://becarioprecario.bitbucket.io/inla-gitbook/ch-priors.html#sec:priors> and the below that the default prior for the log precision (
=log(1/σ2η)) is loggamma:

inla.models()$latent$iid$hyper$theta$name
## [1] "log precision"
## attr(,"inla.read.only")
## [1] FALSE
inla.models()$latent$iid$hyper$theta$prior
## [1] "loggamma"
## attr(,"inla.read.only")
## [1] FALSE
inla.models()$latent$iid$hyper$theta$param
## [1] 1e+00 5e-05
## attr(,"inla.read.only")
## [1] FALSE

The parametrization is described here <https://inla.r-inla-download.org/r-inla.org/doc/prior/prior-loggamma.pdf>:

Drawing from the prior for ση gives:
precision_s = rgamma(n = 1000, shape = 1, rate = 0.00005)
sigma_eta_s = 1/sqrt(precision_s)
ggplot(tibble(sigma_eta_s), aes(x=sigma_eta_s)) + geom_histogram()

Is this correct?

Thanks so much!

Shira

