Raja undulata is an important fishery resource in Portuguese waters. Currently data required for estimating abundance of the species is derived from a self-sampling program conducted by fishermen.

The information collected number of specimens caught by fishing haul and geographic coordinates of the fishing haul. Previously fishermen also provided data of hauls for which no specimens of

Raja undulata was collected. Using former data N-mixture models were applied to get abundance estimates as well as estimates of detection probability (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/316679852_Estimating_animal_abundance_with_N-mixture_models_using_the_R-INLA_package_for_R).

Regarding more recent data for which only  positive fishing haul ae available, i.e., fishing hauls where the species was caught, we would like to know if there are methodological procedures in line with this change.

Waiting to hear from you Thanks

